// scrml.dev /reference/errors/E-PURE-001 — Day-30 placeholder stub

<page>

    // REFERENCE SIDEBAR opt-in — static, page-scoped, zero JS. The nav is
    // authored once in app.scrml and hidden by default; this shows it and
    // marks THIS page's link active. See scripts/gen-reference-nav.mjs.
    #{
        /* !important is load-order, not laziness: the shell's app.css is linked
           AFTER this page's stylesheet, so its `.refnav{display:none}` default
           wins at equal specificity. */
        .ref-shell { display: grid !important; }
        .refnav { display: block !important; }
        .refnav-link[data-ref="errors/E-PURE-001"] {
            color: rgb(125 211 252);
            background-color: rgb(14 165 233 / 0.10);
            border-left-color: rgb(56 189 248);
            font-weight: 600;
        }
    }

    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-3xl">

        // RETIREMENT NOTICE — added by the prose-vs-SPEC audit 2026-07-22.
        // SPEC's diagnostics table carries this code STRUCK THROUGH:
        //   "~~E-PURE-001~~ … Retired 2026-07-16 (S263). Superseded by the
        //    E-FN-001..009 family (§33.6 defines them as specialized
        //    subcategories of E-PURE-001); the `pure` modifier is deprecated
        //    language-wide (use `fn`)."
        // The compiler emits NO E-PURE-001 — grep of compiler/src confirms zero
        // occurrences, while E-FN-001..005/007/008 are all live. The page is kept
        // as a tombstone because old build output and old code still name it.
        <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-md border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3">
            <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 mb-1">
                Retired code
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                <code class="font-mono">E-PURE-001</code> was
                <strong>retired 2026-07-16</strong> and is no longer emitted by
                the compiler. It is superseded by the
                <code class="font-mono">E-FN-001&hellip;009</code> family, which
                SPEC &sect;33.6 defines as specialized subcategories of it. The
                <code class="font-mono">pure</code> modifier is deprecated
                language-wide &mdash; use <code class="font-mono">fn</code>.
                This page is kept because older build output and existing code
                still reference the old code.
            </p>
        </div>


        <header class="not-prose mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 mb-2">
                Reference &rsaquo; Errors
            </div>
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-rose-700 font-mono">
                E-PURE-001
            </h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 mt-2">
                pure-marked function performs a non-pure operation (write, IO, mutation).
            </p>
            <div class="flex gap-3 mt-4 text-xs">
                <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-rose-50 text-rose-700 rounded font-semibold">
                    Error
                </span>
                <a href="https://github.com/bryanmaclee/scrmlTS/blob/main/compiler/SPEC.md#§34"
                   class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                    SPEC §34 (catalogue)
                </a>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="rounded-lg border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-5 py-4 text-slate-800">
            <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">
                Per-code reference page queued for the Day-30 build-out.
            </p>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
                The full template (what it means &middot; minimal reproducer &middot;
                how to fix &middot; related &middot; specification) is being
                rolled out across every error code the compiler can emit.
                Until this page lands, the catalogue row in
                <a href="https://github.com/bryanmaclee/scrmlTS/blob/main/compiler/SPEC.md#§34"
                   class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                    SPEC §34
                </a>
                is authoritative.
            </p>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-10 text-sm">
            <a hard href="/reference" class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                &larr; Reference
            </a>
        </p>

    </article>

</>
